public static void applyWhere(final INDArray to, final Condition condition, final Number number) {
    if (condition instanceof BaseCondition) {
        Nd4j.getExecutioner().exec(new CompareAndSet(to, number.doubleValue(), condition));
    } else {
        double value = number.doubleValue();
        Function<Number, Number> dynamic = new Function<Number, Number>() {
            @Override
            public Number apply(Number number) {
                return value;
            }
        };
        Shape.iterate(to, new CoordinateFunction() {
            @Override
            public void process(long[]... coord) {
                if (condition.apply(to.getDouble(coord[0]))) {
                    to.putScalar(coord[0], dynamic.apply(to.getDouble(coord[0])).doubleValue());
                }
            }
        });
    }
}


**Summary:**
The `applyWhere` method applies a condition to an `INDArray` and sets the elements that meet the condition to a specified number. If the condition is a static condition, it uses a native execution method. Otherwise, it iterates over the array, checks each element against the condition, and updates the element if the condition is met.

