static private void addToMenu(JMenu menu, Preferences prefs) throws BackingStoreException {
    if (debug) System.out.println(" addMenu " + prefs.name());
    String[] keys = prefs.keys();
    for (String key : keys) {
        boolean bval = prefs.getBoolean(key, false);
        String fullname = prefs.absolutePath() + "/" + key;
        menu.add(new DebugMenuItem(fullname, key, bval)); // menu leaf
        if (debug) System.out.println("   leaf= <" + key + "><" + fullname + ">");
    }
    String[] kidName = prefs.childrenNames();
    for (String aKidName : kidName) {
        Preferences pkid = prefs.node(aKidName);
        JMenu subMenu = new JMenu(pkid.name());
        menu.add(subMenu);
        addToMenu(subMenu, pkid);
    }
}


**Summary:**
The `addToMenu` method recursively populates a `JMenu` with items from a `Preferences` object. It iterates through the keys of the `Preferences` object, adding each key as a `DebugMenuItem` to the menu. If the `Preferences` object has child nodes, it creates a sub-menu for each child and recursively calls `addToMenu` on the sub-menu. The method also prints debug information if `debug` is true.

