public static boolean print(String command, Writer out, ucar.nc2.util.CancelTask ct) throws IOException {
    // Extract the filename from the command
    StringTokenizer stoke = new StringTokenizer(command);
    if (!stoke.hasMoreTokens()) {
        out.write(usage);
        return false;
    }
    String filename = stoke.nextToken();

    try (NetcdfFile nc = NetcdfDataset.openFile(filename, ct)) {
        // Process the rest of the command
        int pos = command.indexOf(filename);
        command = command.substring(pos + filename.length());
        return print(nc, command, out, ct);
    } catch (FileNotFoundException e) {
        out.write("file not found= ");
        out.write(filename);
        return false;
    } finally {
        out.close();
    }
}


**Summary:**
The `print` method processes a command string to extract a filename and then attempts to open the corresponding NetCDF file using `NetcdfDataset.openFile`. If successful, it processes the remaining part of the command. If the file is not found, it writes an error message to the output. The method ensures that the output writer is closed in the `finally` block.

