public static boolean conformable(int[] shapeA, int[] shapeB) {
    if (reducedRank(shapeA) != reducedRank(shapeB)) return false;
    int rankB = shapeB.length;
    int dimB = 0;
    for (int aShapeA : shapeA) {
        if (aShapeA == 1) continue;
        while (dimB < rankB) {
            if (shapeB[dimB] == 1) dimB++;
            else break;
        }
        if (aShapeA != shapeB[dimB]) return false;
        dimB++;
    }
    return true;
}


**Summary:**
The `conformable` method checks if two shapes (represented as arrays of integers) are conformable. It first ensures that the reduced ranks of both shapes are the same. Then, it iterates through each dimension of the first shape, skipping dimensions of length 1. For each non-skipped dimension, it finds the corresponding dimension in the second shape, skipping dimensions of length 1 as well. If any dimension does not match, it returns `false`. If all dimensions match, it returns `true`.

