public static String stripLastWord(String prefix) {
    if (prefix.isEmpty()) {
        return prefix;
    }
    if (prefix.charAt(prefix.length() - 1) == ' ') {
        return "";
    } else {
        char[] c = prefix.toCharArray();
        int start = 0;
        for (int i = c.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            if (Character.isWhitespace(c[i])) {
                start = i + 1;
                break;
            }
        }
        prefix = prefix.substring(start, prefix.length());
        return prefix;
    }
}


**Summary:**
The `stripLastWord` method removes the last word from a given string `prefix`. If the string is empty or ends with a space, it returns the string as is. Otherwise, it iterates from the end of the string to find the first whitespace character, then returns the substring from the start of the string to the position just after the whitespace.

