public static void vertexAverage(Polygon2D_F64 input, Point2D_F64 average) {
    average.setIdx(0, 0);
    for (int i = 0; i < input.size(); i++) {
        Point2D_F64 v = input.vertexes.data[i];
        average.x += v.x;
        average.y += v.y;
    }
    average.x /= input.size();
    average.y /= input.size();
}


**Summary:**
This method calculates the average of the vertices of a 2D polygon. It initializes the average point to (0,0), then iterates through each vertex of the polygon, adding the x and y coordinates to the average. Finally, it divides the total x and y coordinates by the number of vertices to get the average coordinates, which are stored in the `average` point.

